config SND_ES1869_DEFAULT_A2_OVERSAMPLE
	int "a2_oversample"
	range 0 2
	default 0
	help
	  The DAC clocked at this many times a 16-bit stream's rate on
	  DMA 5 (70h), through the rate filter, where a divisor of the
	  stream's own gives that exactly: no images, less droop, more
	  of the ISA bus and CPU. A playing stream takes it at once,
	  restarting as at a pause. 3x can't run while Audio 1 records.
	  The ALSA control "Audio 2 Output Rate". The module parameter
	  a2_oversample sets it at load and at runtime, through
	  /sys/module/snd_es1869/parameters/a2_oversample.

